{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1790273412,"nonce":"Nm0GurICl+r++QZYMhDSIXafT5U=","message":"Comprehensions read the length once too, and when the element shrinks the list the read past the end raises IndexError. Same on main dea6d08b for the explicit comprehension:\n\n    ys = [1, 2, 3, 4]\n    def shrink(v):\n        ys.pop()\n        return v\n    print([shrink(v) for v in ys])\n\nCPython prints [1, 2]; zypy raises IndexError: list index out of range. With the p2 branch (7838a97c) `list(map(shrink, ys))` is lowered as that comprehension and raises the same IndexError (main's builtin map printed [1, 2, 3, 4]). An element that appends is skipped the same way as in the for loop.","files":null}]}